<!-- ABOUT -->
<section id="about">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="sec-head"><span class="idx">01</span><h2>About</h2></div>
    <div class="about-grid">
      <div class="about">
        <p>I'm a Space Engineering student at York University's Lassonde School of Engineering and an aspiring propulsion engineer. I like problems that sit between the physics and the wrench — CAD and analysis on one side, machining and test-stand assembly on the other.</p>
        <p>I co-lead <strong>Arbalest Rocketry</strong>, where I've designed payload thermal hardware, contributed to PCB design, machined flight components, and secured team sponsorship. I've run independent research on lunar-dust mitigation for Artemis-era missions and presented it at the Canadian Space Conference. I hold a prior <strong>Engineering Physics</strong> degree from Istanbul Technical University, train as a <strong>Scientist-Astronaut Candidate</strong> with the IIAS, and am working toward my pilot's license.</p>
        <p>Alongside the engineering, I work as a medical interpreter across six languages, and I organize outreach like <strong>Rising Beyond Gravity</strong> to bring more women into aerospace. My long-term goal is to work in propulsion and nuclear energy for spaceflight — and, one day, to fly myself.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="facts">
        <div class="fact"><div class="k">Career focus</div><div class="v">Propulsion · nuclear energy · human spaceflight</div></div>
        <div class="fact"><div class="k">Based in</div><div class="v">North York, Ontario, Canada</div></div>
        <div class="fact"><div class="k">Tools</div><div class="v">SolidWorks · KiCad · MATLAB · Python · LabVIEW</div></div>
        <div class="fact"><div class="k">Hands-on</div><div class="v">Machining (mill/lathe) · PCB &amp; circuits · test stands</div></div>
        <div class="fact"><div class="k">Languages</div><div class="v">English · Turkish · Farsi · Pashto · Urdu/Hindi · Azeri</div></div>
      </div>
    </div>

